sections.text:
A relation r is an equivalence relation if

it is reflexive: for all x, r(x, x) is true;
 it is symmetric: for all a and b, r(a, b) is true if and only if r(b, a) is true;
 it is transitive: r(a, b) && r(b, c) implies r(a, c).

examples.code:
#include <concepts>
#include <functional>
#include <cassert>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    // The compiler verifies this requirement before the program runs.
    static_assert(std::equivalence_relation<std::equal_to<>, int, int>);
    std::cout << "Checks passed\n";
}
